        "THGOV-CABINET-SSO-2025",
        "RD-RC-SECTION-38-64",
        "RD-DEDUCTION-SCHEDULE"
      ],
      "review_notes": [
        "Tax deduction uses actual contributions paid; the statutory wage base is used only to calculate a contribution when requested.",
        "The cabinet summary confirms the 17,500 baht ceiling applies to B.E. 2569-2571 (2026-2028), the 1,650 baht floor is unchanged, and the rate remains 5%, giving a 875 baht monthly maximum.",
        "Direct Royal Gazette, volume 142 part 81 A, 12 December 2025, printed page 5 clauses 1 and 3(1); visually verified from PDF on 2026-10-15. Original PDF SHA-256: 529c7de6cbf8697e4777e1489639b60833131abece6f9bb7e7778c6ad3f6b07b. See docs/policy-evidence/2026-10-15/README.md. No tax constants changed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "rule_id": "TH-PIT-ALLOWANCE-PARENT",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "tax_year": 2026,
      "effective_from": "2026-01-01",
      "effective_to": "2026-12-31",
      "status": "EFFECTIVE",
      "source_id": "RD-RC-SECTION-38-64",
      "verified_at": "2026-09-15",
      "parameters": {
        "amount_per_eligible_parent": "30000.00"
      },
      "supplementary_source_ids": [
        "RD-DEDUCTION-SCHEDULE"
      ],
      "review_notes": [
        "Eligibility is supplied explicitly; this phase does not infer it.",
        "The published schedule conditions this allowance on a parent aged 60 or over whose assessable income does not exceed 30,000 baht; those statutory conditions are caller-asserted in this phase."
      ]
    },
    {
